methods=[
('USDA sources and table locations','The analysis uses the 2013, 2018 and 2023 Census of Aquaculture as three repeated cross sections. Table 7 (printed page 10 in each report) supplies national commercial-category and food or market-size sales fields. Table 19 supplies all-size national and state clam farm counts and sales; relevant printed pages are 46-48 in 2013 and 44-46 in 2018 and 2023. The raw archive includes unchanged standalone tables, complete reports, appendices and native 2018/2023 CSV files verified against their official ZIP members. The corrected 2018 sources reside under the USDA 2017 AgCensus directory, not the 2022 directory. URLs, exact PDF pages, file hashes and used fields are recorded in RAW_DATA_MANIFEST.csv.'),
('Commercial categories and census comparability','Primary groups are Hard clams (questionnaire code 2), Manila clams (3) and Geoducks (4). Other clams (5) is a residual commercial group, not a fixed species. Eastern oysters (12), Pacific oysters (13) and Mussels (9) are descriptive industry references. Codes are interpreted within the year-specific mollusk questionnaire section. The 2023 code 12 form wording is Eastern/Gulf Coast; published Table 7 retains Eastern. Original questionnaires, USDA appendices on comparability and the 2023 USDA questionnaire update hosted by NASDA document the reporting labels. These sources support published commercial group comparisons; they do not establish exclusive and unchanged biological species, product quality or farm populations.'),
('Extraction and human verification','The pipeline extracts all six Table 7 fields from page text, retaining every original token, page, line, category and stage. State rows are parsed from their Table 19 column groups, retaining national rows for reconciliation. Original 2018/2023 CSV checks locate Table 7 by its title rather than by a misleading component filename. Table 7 all-size clam farms and sales are checked against Table 19; state farm sums are independently checked against national totals. All relevant numeric source pages and questionnaire pages require visual verification. Scanned form pages are not claimed to be fully interpreted by text extraction. No manually keyed numeric analysis table is required by the pipeline; page images and review records are retained in internal QC.'),
('Suppression and missing values','D is USDA disclosure suppression and remains a non-numeric value. X remains not applicable. A published dash is distinguished from a missing field and retained as the original symbol; for farm counts only it is represented as the official zero or rounds-to-zero estimate. Sales dashes are not silently filled with zero. No D values are estimated from totals, other size stages, other years or neighboring states. Manila 2018 market-size sales, Mussels 2013 sales and all three Other-clam market-size sales are D. Unavailable endpoint comparisons remain explicit NA rows.'),
('CPI adjustment','Annual average CPI-U is extracted from period M13 of archived official BLS API JSON for series CUUR0000SA0: all items, U.S. city average, not seasonally adjusted, 1982-84=100. The annual values are 232.957 (2013), 251.107 (2018) and 304.702 (2023). Constant 2023-dollar V equals nominal V multiplied by CPI2023/CPIyear. The same factor applies to P. CPI-U measures general purchasing power; it is not an aquaculture-specific output price index. No CPI values are substituted for the raw API chain.'),
('Matching sales unit values','Within a commercial group, census and food/market-size stage, V is published nominal sales in thousand USD and Q is live-weight sales in thousand lb. P=V/Q therefore has units USD/lb. Q is whole live weight sold at that stage, not total aquaculture production. The unrounded ratio of the published V and Q values is retained for calculation. All-size sales are never paired with market-size weight. Different group counts of animals sold are not added. Derived unit values include changing product and farm composition and are not quality-adjusted prices.'),
('Symmetric arithmetic decomposition','For each prespecified endpoint comparison, quantity contribution CQ=(Q1-Q0)(P0+P1)/2 and unit-value contribution CU=(P1-P0)(Q0+Q1)/2. Their sum equals V1-V0. The pipeline calculates nominal and constant 2023-dollar versions separately. Internal values use thousand USD, while tables and figures use million USD of the indicated basis. All seven candidate commercial groups, all three endpoint comparisons and both monetary bases are retained in Table S2, including unavailable comparisons. Components are arithmetic identities, not estimates of causal demand, price or efficiency mechanisms.'),
('Precision and publication rounding','Calculations use full machine precision without rounding intermediate V/Q. An independent 45-digit Decimal calculation uses raw printed V, Q and CPI tokens, with an alternative algebraic decomposition. Published V and Q are treated as rounded to whole thousands and official mean values as rounded to cents when checking interval overlap. The 16 endpoint combinations using V and Q plus or minus 0.5 published unit are evaluated for each identified comparison. Component extrema and unit-value percentage extrema are reported in Table S3. This is finite publication-rounding sensitivity only, not a 95 percent confidence interval or a bound on survey error. Official mean values are not forced to equal the ratio of separately rounded totals.'),
('State reporting farms','Table S4 retains all 50 states, four clam categories and three censuses (600 records). Farm counts cover all sizes and can overlap across categories. Figure S1 displays the union of states with a positive published farm estimate in any of the three censuses for any of the three primary groups. It never selects only 2023 states. The original dash is shown for published zero/rounds-to-zero farm estimates. Confidential sales remain D and are not used to assign a false zero color. These are reporting distributions, not enterprise ownership concentration, biological ranges, tracked farm entry/exit or geographic production estimates.'),
('Scope and limits','This descriptive study has three census observations, not a continuous annual panel. Changes in reporting operations are not changes within identified farms. Same-group V/Q comparability does not remove changing size, quality, geography or sales-channel composition. Suppression prevents some endpoint comparisons and most complete state sales analyses. Reference shellfish are not independent causal controls. No regressions, significance tests, interpolations, imputed years, mechanistic claims or new research directions are added. The manuscript must retain its core source, matching, CPI and decomposition methods; this supplement supplies technical details rather than replacing main-text Methods.')]
